From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 00:16:48 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 282/342] freebsd_network: don't release the PCI module twice

A USB driver's PCI scan finds nothing and calls uninit_pci(), and unloading the
driver calls it again, with gPci still set. On x86 others hold the module, so
nothing happens. On the ODROID-C2 nobody else does: the reference count of this
B_KEEP_LOADED module dropped to 0 and the kernel panicked, when a realtekwifi
that was in use was deleted from the non-packaged folder.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/libs/compat/freebsd_network/pci.cpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/libs/compat/freebsd_network/pci.cpp b/src/libs/compat/freebsd_network/pci.cpp
index 774b8b378a..be17519d5d 100644
--- a/src/libs/compat/freebsd_network/pci.cpp
+++ b/src/libs/compat/freebsd_network/pci.cpp
@@ -42,8 +42,10 @@ init_pci()
 void
 uninit_pci()
 {
-	if (gPci != NULL)
+	if (gPci != NULL) {
 		put_module(B_PCI_MODULE_NAME);
+		gPci = NULL;
+	}
 }
 
 
